      ":question/problem": "Express $1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{2\\pi}{5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
